This post comes roughly 5 days since my last ascension post. I was 
criticised for breaking all conducts and taking over 70,000 turns. I decided 
to try a wizard this time (never played them before). It took me about 30 
quick and early deaths before I had a solid character going. It's really a 
lot different than a straight-up melee Valk or Sam. I finally gave in and 
put a bunch of metal armor on. It really helps you survive in the early game 
until you can get Magicbane or a wish. If you're chaotic, you might try my 
technique of offing a Watchman in the Mine Town. BUC test it and you'll end 
up with some decent armor pieces.

This game is under 1/2 the turns my last 2 ascensions were. This time I 
decided to go genoless as well. That decision almost cost me but I stuck 
with it. When I broke into Rodney's shack, he had a hissy fit and summoned a 
bunch of monsters, including a Master-Lich. Then, he stole my Eye of 
Aethiopica. This is where it started to go downhill. I cast Finger of Death 
on Rodney at least 5-6 times, and he resisted it each time. By this time I 
was quite flooded with enemies around me. I tried to manipulate Rodney so I 
wouldn't have to kill him in the water, and then, oh boy, DOUBLE TROUBLE. At 
this moment I had forgotten that it was the Eye that was making me recharge 
energy so fast. So there I was, surrounded by summons with no energy. I 
finally got up enough energy to cast Charm Monster, and lo and behold, the 
spell had timed out and I had forgotten it! I really should have thought it 
over better, but my solution was to wish for a new book of Charm Monster, 
and then relearn it. To do that, I had to teleport a bunch of enemies to 
make a path. The message line was a complete spam fest and I just got fed up 
and kept pressing space to get past it. BAD idea. I didn't notice that a 
cockatrice had been working it's magic, and before I knew it, Amulet of 
Lifesaving #1 went up in smoke. That was the first and only timed I needed 
up, but it was a big wakeup call that I needed to pay more attention. I 
eventually made it into one of the small rooms in the back of the zoo area. 
I engraved Elbereth in the door and dropped a gem on it. I made myself a 
little study room. It was at this time my buddy Mr. L decided to show up. 
With the help of Magicbane, he was stunned over and over and I killed him. 
To make a long story short, I learned CM again and it helped a lot.

After that, I got hit by a mindflayer twice and lost a bunch of memories. I 
also had to deal with 2 liches on astral, but they actually ended up making 
it a lot easier for me. They summoned a bunch of monsters... then I charmed 
the summons! :) CM is definately an amazing spell. There is nothing like 
turning your enemies into your allies.

I'm not too sure I'll go genoless again. The liches proved to be extremely 
aggrivating to me, with their warping and summoning hijinx. I dealt with the 
seacreatures a lot more smoothly than I thought I would, and I didn't even 
have an oilskin cloak up until the Plane of Fire when I wished for one. I 
think my next character will be a weaponless conduct monk. I'm not sure how 
well that will go. I'm still really a newbie at Nethack. I haven't even 
played 3/4 of the classes, or even races. Hell, my wizard was the first 
chaotic character I've ever played.

Speaking of Charm Monster, I got a little carried away with the charming in 
Fort Ludios and ended up killing a bunch of my pets with a spell or five. 
Well, god didn't like that, and he took away all my protection. Luckily 
Ludios provided more than enough gold to buy it back, and then some.

Other than that, it was pretty uneventful. Found 2 Hearse bones piles: one 
in the Big Room, and another in the VoD. Both of them had empty wands of 
wishing with 1 recharge left. I found 2 magic lamps up to that point, and 
decided to run them to get a wish for scrolls of charging. The first lamp 
was a dud; the genie left in a puff of smoke. I thought there was no way the 
2nd would do that... It didn't, true: it was even worse. The god damned 
genie attacked me after it came out of the lamp. I am positive they were 
both blessed. What gives?

The Magic Mapping spell made Gehennom bearable. I don't know if I would have 
been able to continue if I had to manually map out ~20 levels of mazes. I 
always get burned out around the time: and this was only my 3rd time there! 
Oh, now that I think of it, I'm 3 for 3 in ascensions after reaching the 
castle; Every character I've gotten past that point has survived. Lucky? 
Probably.

I guess that's it.

